WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:03.670
The electric light, the
telephone, the microchip.

00:00:03.737 --> 00:00:05.105
All great inventions.

00:00:05.171 --> 00:00:06.940
But for me, the most
important of all

00:00:07.006 --> 00:00:12.045
was the wheel, mainly because
it led to things like this.

00:00:12.112 --> 00:00:15.248
Downhill cycling.

00:00:15.315 --> 00:00:18.451
Why use two wheels when one
makes you look twice as cool?

00:00:21.721 --> 00:00:25.992
But before you even think about
pulling off a downhill wheelie,

00:00:26.059 --> 00:00:32.198
be aware that even
on two wheels,

00:00:32.265 --> 00:00:33.566
it could still be perilous.

00:00:36.836 --> 00:00:39.873
What makes downhill cycling
is such a terrifying pursuit

00:00:39.939 --> 00:00:43.309
is that the bike isn't only
powered by the cyclist's legs,

00:00:43.376 --> 00:00:45.412
but also by our
old friend gravity.

00:00:48.481 --> 00:00:51.518
When a cyclist goes up a
hill, he gradually gains

00:00:51.584 --> 00:00:55.288
gravitational potential energy.

00:00:55.355 --> 00:00:58.224
When he descends, this
gravitational potential energy

00:00:58.291 --> 00:01:01.127
can be converted over a
very short period of time

00:01:01.194 --> 00:01:03.363
into a terrifying amount
of kinetic energy.

00:01:06.366 --> 00:01:09.235
If the rider falls, that kinetic
energy might be converted

00:01:09.302 --> 00:01:12.972
into heat via friction,
or if they stop suddenly,

00:01:13.039 --> 00:01:16.910
dissipated via deformation.

00:01:16.976 --> 00:01:19.779
So energy is never destroyed.

00:01:19.846 --> 00:01:21.981
It's merely transferred
into something else

00:01:22.048 --> 00:01:24.651
like kinetic energy,
heat, or even the sound

00:01:24.717 --> 00:01:27.086
of an impact, which
is often accompanied

00:01:27.153 --> 00:01:28.822
by the sound of screaming.

00:01:28.888 --> 00:01:30.890
To investigate, we sent
out some of our more

00:01:30.957 --> 00:01:32.392
reckless researchers.

00:01:35.962 --> 00:01:38.131
This guy has made
a deal with gravity

00:01:38.198 --> 00:01:39.799
and built up a lot
of kinetic energy.

00:01:43.169 --> 00:01:45.472
So much so that he's
able to pass cars.

00:01:52.512 --> 00:01:55.515
Except that one.

00:01:55.582 --> 00:01:57.484
The cyclist is
unable to transfer

00:01:57.550 --> 00:02:01.921
enough kinetic energy into heat
the friction at its brakes.

00:02:01.988 --> 00:02:04.924
When he hits the car, his
remaining kinetic energy

00:02:04.991 --> 00:02:09.762
is transferred into sound, heat,
and dissipated a deformation,

00:02:09.829 --> 00:02:12.265
also known as bouncing off.

00:02:12.332 --> 00:02:13.066
Don't worry.

00:02:13.132 --> 00:02:13.833
He was OK.

00:02:16.269 --> 00:02:17.003
All right.

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:19.105
Let's try a gentler pace.

00:02:19.172 --> 00:02:20.273
This is more like it.

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:21.708
A chance to take in the scenery.

00:02:24.878 --> 00:02:27.580
And his friend's bottom.

00:02:27.647 --> 00:02:31.851
He appears to make no attempt
to reduce his kinetic energy.

00:02:31.918 --> 00:02:35.288
And his linear momentum
becomes angular momentum

00:02:35.355 --> 00:02:37.724
as he rotates around the
axle of the front wheel.

00:02:42.161 --> 00:02:43.563
And maybe not the last.

00:02:50.169 --> 00:02:52.138
Perhaps it's safer to
go downhill on three

00:02:52.205 --> 00:02:53.339
wheels with these drift trikes.

00:02:58.678 --> 00:03:01.047
Or maybe not.

00:03:01.114 --> 00:03:03.049
It's just as well our
drift trike gang are

00:03:03.116 --> 00:03:06.986
heading home on four wheels.

00:03:07.053 --> 00:03:08.054
Maybe safer just to walk.

